#X text 102 391 Windowing functions are used with FFTs. These transform the signal block-by-block into a spectral representation whose resolution in both the frequency and time domains are proportional to their size (as a power-of-two in PD). The different windows have different characteristics in terms of stopband attenuation and noise bandwidth.;
